"The peaceful city is an illusion, a vision of a gentle end laid over the ruins."
"The belltowers and spires are really obelisks of bone, capped with dark crystals."
"Each obelisk crystal is taller than a man and sits nearly half a mile up."
"Together the obelisks form a ritual circle spanning the whole city."
"The circle's spell reaches out to travelers about a dozen miles from the city."
"Struts of bone bridge the city's ancient buildings."
"The city's forest is of bone-and-vein trees whose fruit are undead."
"The bone forest begins a few miles out from the ring of hills."
